decisions.inWild:
A request router can try ordered thresholds and readiness checks in one table:
```jet
if queue_depth < _ {
    8 && primary_ready -> route_primary()
    32 && (secondary_ready || emergency) -> route_secondary()
    else -> reject_request()
}
```
The values 8 and 32 fill the same typed hole. Each extra Boolean check applies to that arm. This is a proposed usage example, not an observed production deployment.

